    <string name="ram_zram_header">Compressed RAM (zram)</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_caption">Apps you are not using get squeezed to about a third of their size and stay in RAM, so more of them stay open. Starts after a restart.</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_title">%1$d%% · %2$s GB</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_desc_25">Least work for the processor, fewer apps kept</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_desc_50">A good balance</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_desc_75">More apps stay open</string>
    <string name="ram_zram_desc_100">The most apps, for a little more processor work</string>

    <string name="ram_wb_header">Swap to storage</string>
    <string name="ram_wb_caption">Once a day, while the phone is idle, apps you have not touched for hours move from compressed RAM to a file on storage. Opening them again takes a moment longer. It uses free storage and wears it a little, so it is off unless you turn it on. Starts after a restart.</string>
